{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1456297-trinity-core-they-came-from-beneath-the-sea-style-stunts-in-trinity-continuum","id":1456297,"title":"[Trinity Core] They Came from Beneath the Sea! style stunts in Trinity Continuum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-07T05:24:31-07:00","id":1456297,"title":"[Trinity Core] They Came from Beneath the Sea! style stunts in Trinity Continuum?","content":"I just picked up another Storypath system, They Came from Beneath the Sea! (Side note, pick it up. It's phenomenal). It's a Storypath system at the end of the day, so there's a lot of similarities. I expected there to be system differences, but the way they handle stunts almost seems a direct upgrade over Trinity Continuum.<br /> <br /> See, they have the same three basic stunts. Enhance, complicate, and defend; however, they also have a huge list of stunts. These stunts are then broken down by general stunts anyone can use and stunts specific to archetypes. These lists are further broken down by cost from 1 success to 3 successes. You don't have to purchase these like skill tricks. All characters just have access to these as long as they roll the proper successes, match the archetype, and meet the narrative requirements.<br /> <br /> I see this as the perfect opportunity for a Storypath Nexus product. Aside from generating a list of stunts, my thought next is how to break these down. Trinity doesn't have classes/archetypes in the way They Came From does. I don't want to split this up by skills and even splitting by attribute seems dicey with 9 lists. My next thoughts:<br /> <br /> Split by area: Three lists, physical, social, and mental. Three lists isn't monstrous and could even give extra time to fluff out those lists.<br /> Split by role: I'd select a few key Role Paths. Enough to cover a broad range of character archetypes. They Came From has five, so I suppose I'd also try to find five. Lists could be generated for a few initial role paths. If you create your own path, you could then mix and match stunts to create your own list. Let's say you had the role path of a Fighter to represent a famed celebrity martial artist. You could take two stunts from Combat Specialist and two stunts from Celebrity to create the new list for your desired path. Again, these are all magic numbers. I'm just spitballing. No idea how long the final list would be if this was created.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26906-jeffreybezos","name":"JeffreyBezos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T05:40:51-07:00","id":1456298,"title":"","content":"My suggestion is to split into kinds of situation you can use, combat stunts, investigation stunt, hacking stunts, stealth stunts, etc etc.<br /> <br /> It may be a lot of work, but it can be helpful for sure.<br /> <br /> Personally, I try to suggest people to \u201cfree form\u201d stunts in the fly, asking GM for cost and possibility, but it\u2019s far more difficult than one may expect, even in the most common situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}